Hi,

I don't know if this will help, but I have installed Redhat 7.0 on a Jensen,
so I would imagine that a multi would be supported, as the Jensen is even
older. I now have Redhat 7.0 updated running on my Jensen, and it runs
great. I had problems with a few things before with Redhat, but now i've put
7.0 on it,they have all disapperaed, and it runs great. I installed it using
the hard disk drive, with the cd iso's contents written on the second hard
disk in the system. I've installed Redhat 6.2 over ftp, though using a cd in
another drive on another machine on my small LAN, as i don't have a
permanent net connection, so getting disconnected every 2 hours on a 56k
would really cause problems. :-)  If you have any questions about how I
installed it, ask me on or off the mailing list.

Graeme Hogg

