On Sun, 10 Jun 2001, Andri Saar wrote:

> 
> 
> Kurt Ludwig wrote:
> > 
> > might also be the memory that is in it. did you try swapping it yet?
> > 
> > also it may be the cache on the motherboard. if it's that, then you're kinda
> > stuck living with the ECC errors.
> > 
> 
> Memory is brand-new, and worked in another Alpha just like a charm.
> 
> Can I disable the L3 cache somehow and see if I don't get those errors?
> 
> Still, with AlphaBIOS+MILO (yes, don't say it's evil, I want to see if I
> can get Linux working and then I'll do a decent install) I managed to
> boot up, and still get various errors.
> 
> For example, if I do a `w' I get the following errior:
> 
> w(PID): unaligned trap at 00000001200016c0: 00000011ff786 2c 31
> w(PID): unaligned trap at 00000001200016c4: 00000011ff78a 2c 31
> w(PID): unaligned trap at 00000001200016c8: 00000011ff78e 2c 31
> w(PID): unaligned trap at 00000001200016cc: 00000011ff792 2c 31

That's software, not a hardware problem.
 
> and when I switch consoles (alt+f2, alt+f1): 
> 
> PYXIS machine check: vector=0x660 pc=0xfffffc00003103a0 code=0x202
> machine check type: unknown

That's a hardware problem....you could try disabling the cache and seeing
if that fixes the machine checks, it will of course effect performance,
but at least you could narrow it down.

--rdp

-- 
