On Mon, 11 Jun 2001, Peter Bech wrote:

-> All I recall was (v6.2) something like this:
-> 
-> cd /usr/src/redhat
-> make xconfig

He means that you should recompile the kernel
and configure it for another alpha processor, perhaps
a generic one.
After 'make xconfig' you'll need to do a lot of work,
and it will take you more than the five minutes you have :-(
(unless you have another maniche to do the job...)

You said that the same machine works with FreeBSD?
I'm asking because it sounds like a tipical overheating
problem... everything works fine for 5 min.

Usualy during the instalation process the processor type is
recognized and if it isn't linux uses a kernel for a generic
(alpha) processor, so i don't think you need to recompile
the kernel.

regards, nelson




