<html><mailto:axp-list-request@redhat.com?subject=help><mailto:axp-list@redhat.com><mailto:axp-list-request@redhat.com?subject=subscribe><mailto:axp-list-request@redhat.com?subject=unsubscribe>
<DIV></DIV>
<P>My experiences on my XL366 with Matrox Millenium II .</P>
<P>Mine has Three partitions</P>
<P>1. /dev/sda1 DOS boot partition where milo and linload.exe will be placed after install to facilitate booting from hard disk.</P>
<P>2. /dev/sda2&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; /&nbsp;&nbsp; partition</P>
<P>3. /dev/sda3&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; swap</P>
<P>MILO: I have found using the milo image from Redhat6.2 works, RH7.0 milos don't work similar problem to yours.</P>
<P>You need to use the kernel and ramdisk floppies...RH7 doesn't support booting from the CD with Alphabios.</P>
<P>Kernel and Ramdisk from RH7.0 work on mine. You have to use these else it will not recognise the RH7 CD rom in the drive. </P>
<P>&nbsp;I assume you are using</P>
<P>MILO&gt; boot fd0:vmlinux.gz root=/dev/fd0 load_ramdisk=1</P>
<P>I remember starting out also having load_prompt = 1 and for some reason it wouldn't boot the kernel disk properly.</P>
<P>This gets me to the install no problem or you can put in "text" at the end for text mode. Can mount the CDROM drive too.</P>
<P>Do you have the latest formware for the XL366 think its about 5.69 from memory?</P>
<P>Have you had any version of linux installed before?</P>
<P>&nbsp;</P>
<P>Cheers,</P>
<P>&nbsp;</P>
<P>James</P>
