There was some discussion about a year ago on the list about this (as I
asked the same question).  It came back from those that know (and this is
what I have been running now for close to a year) that you need ECC SDRAM,
unbuffered, 83Mhz or greater.  They have to be installed in pairs (memory
bus width).  The max memory is 1.5GB on the board (three pairs = 512MB per
stick max).  I didn't get crucial memory (more than I had to spend).  I
did get brand name though, as advised by the list.  Just to be safe.

I hope that helps.  If you have questions, please let me know.
James



