Are there any benchmarks available comparing intel with alpha, using the
same compiler under linux?  I appreciate the fact that one compiler may be
better than another, but an apples to aplles comparison, I would find
interesting.  The frequency of the underlying cpu is irrelvant since that
can be scaled.  what is more important is to extract the instruction set
strength, which could best be accomplished using,e.g., gcc without
optimization on both systems.  FP performance is not important for such a
measure, but is yet another test that is interesting.

Tom

