gcc intel != gcc alpha

Or I could be wrong.  I figure that the work that has gone into 
optimization on the two platforms differ.  So what does it matter
if it is the same compiler?  Ok, so you do use optimiziations.  Different
platforms are going to have different code generators.   

You should compare the 'best' compiler on one platform to the 'best' compiler 
on the other.  Why use gcc if the Compaq compilers are much better?  It 
depends on the tests that you care about.  I could care less if an 
unoptimized gcc runs faster on an Athlon than an Alpha.  I care what
is the absolute fastest I can make my code go on each platform.

