On Wed, 20 Jun 2001, Linus Gasser wrote:

-> Hi,
-> I tried yesterday to install the newest RawHide7.1-tree. But as I have an 
-> AlphaBios-machine, I couldn't install it in any way. Under RH7.0 there was a 
-> milo/ directory, which seems to be missing in RawHide. Did anyone manage to 

You can copy milo into your hard disk. You just need to creat a dos
partition and write milo there... then you can install what dist. you
want i don't need to care about milo anymore (unless you need to upgrade it).
I had my machines in this way for a long time! but since i've been told
that they have SRM (thank you Michal Jaegermann), i boot them via SRM, and i feel
more happy :-)

You have some docs regarding SRM and aboot at www.alphalinux.org.

regards, nelson

P.S. with milo you need linload.exe too. As far as i remember you need to make a floppy
disk with linload and milo, and somehow (there's some magic here), you write loadlin
in the dos partition - see in the alphabios! then you can copy milo...




