However, you'll find that the new Alpha backend in gcc 2.96 as shipped
with Red Hat Linux 7.1 is quite competitive in the Alpha optimization
space.  We did the new backend under contract with Alpha Processor,
Inc.  Compaq loved showing demos at trade shows of a povray built with
gcc in one window, and ccc in another.  ccc was always winning.  When
I had them rebuild their povray with 2.96 with the correct compiler
flags (-mcpu=ev67 -O6 -mieee -fomit-frame-pointer, etc) ccc only had a
*slight* edge over gcc.  And you can use gcc for commercial usage...

Cheers,

Matt

(of course, advances in gcc could drive innovation in ccc --
competition is Good.)

