> On the other hand the dependencies mean that the libs are currently
> installed. Why would the new glibc overwrite them if they are separate
> packages? 

It's the other way around.  Older glibc releases included db1 and db2 (and 
maybe db3).  Since you now remove the older glibc, you need to add the now 
independant packages containing db[123].  You should be able to find them on 
any redhat mirror (they'll probably be marked for redhat 7.x).

