On Wed, Jun 20, 2001 at 03:20:01PM +0200, Peter Mittermayer wrote:
> 
> > OK.. then it's about time to install RedHat 7.0 instead of RedHat 6.2 !
> > 
> 
> No prob. You could wait a few days. I thinkt RH7.1 for alpha will be out
> by then. At least some others seem to think so :) But I do not know if
> the Compaq compilers will run on 7.1 as well.

They will.  The only thing is that for some reasons 'ccc', but not
'fort', does not like when LANG environment variable is set and it
complains before getting to work.  If you want to avoid that make
yourself an alias, or a shell wrapper, called also 'ccc' which unsets
LANG before calling "the real thing".  Or unset LANG globally but you
may not want to do that for other reasons.

gcc and g77 are also not exactly an old egcs with which you are likely
familiar.

  Michal




