Hello,
I am trying to install an ATI XPert 98 video card
(PCI) that is listed in
the redhat.com alpha hardware compatibility list in my
digital workstation
500 au. SRM complains when I do this, and it says...
 
"Illegal device detected on primary bus in physical
slot 4 Power down the
system and remove the unsupported device from slot 4"
 
I tried to see if alphabios would recognize it. It did
not like the card
either. I pretty recently upgraded my bios to the
latest available i.e.,
SRM firmware V7.2-1. Please let me know how I can work
around this.
 
Also, I previously had a powerstorm series video card
that I could not get
Xconfigurator to recognize. Has anybody been
successful with those cards?
 
 
Thanks.
John

