Dear Jay and alpha lists participants:

Thanks for the advice regarding my problem with PYXIS
machine checks w/1.5GB RAM...

I've built a new 2.2.19pre7 kernel using the
Debianized source and still receive these machine
checks:-(

The vendor checked these 256MB DIMMs and found no
errors.

Strangely enough, I don't receive these machine checks
under DU4.0e, nor when I install only 512MB (2 DIMMs)
under Debian.  The machine checks reoccur when I've
got 1024MB (4 DIMMs) installed (again, under Debian).

I'm considering obtaining DEC-branded 256MB DIMMs to
see if these machine checks still occur.

My questions:
1.  Is this a worthwhile thing to do?
2.  Is this strictly a Linux kernel problem with
	PYXIS - if so, will this be resolved?
3.  Has anyone successfully used 1.5GB RAM in a
	DEC -a/-au series Personal Workstation?

Many thanks,
sousa

----------------------------------------------------
