> Miata... 
> 
> My question: does the Linux kernel (on the Debian
2.2 
> boot disks) have trouble addressing large amounts of

> RAM? Or is my new memory possibly defective? Has 
> anyone encountered this before? 

There was a problem a while ago, with PYXIS support
(MIATA/LX/SX) 
being limited to 1GB of RAM. Not a problem on LX/SX,
since they have 
only 4 DIMM slots, but MIATA has 6... :-\ 

This was fixed... :-) 

Please try (since you've tried 2.2.16 and 2.2.17 :-)
2.2.18 or, 
better, 2.2.19. 

Good luck. 

