Friends:

I just got around to upgrading my lx164 from RH6.1 to RH7.0 (6.1 
was working fine, but the security people think that apache/ftp 
need better security outside the firewall).

The lx164 has a 3Com Vortex card (3c905) which has run well for 
three years using Don Becker's 3c59x driver as a module.  The 
networking is set up for manual configuration.  So once RH7.0 is 
up, eth0 fails on start up. ifconfig only shows localhost lo.  I can't 
believe I fried the card (especially as I did an ftp-upgrade) so I am 
somehow misconfigured.  Any suggestions?  Do I need to build my 
own kernel?

Cheers,
Will


