> On Thu, 28 Jun 2001, Ingo T. Storm wrote:
> 
> > >The lx164 has a 3Com Vortex card (3c905) which has run well for
> > >three years using Don Becker's 3c59x driver as a module.  The
> > >networking is set up for manual configuration.  So once RH7.0 is
> > >up, eth0 fails on start up.
> >
> > IIRC correctly, the rh7.0 kernel wants a module name in
> > /etc/modules.conf for this card that is different from the name the
> > older drivers used.
> 
> I'm typing this on an lx164 with a 3c905.  All I have in /etc/modules.conf
> is:
> 
> alias eth0 3c59x
> 
> It's been working fine since I built the box late last year.
